text She runs off to the librarian's desk.
text She takes out the mop and begins cleaning.
text I sit down on a nearby seat and put the key and bag on the table.
text I look at the key's label again.
text "Kotomi"
text The handwriting has large, round letters, as if written by a child.
text I turn my head and look out a window.
text The sunny sky makes the rain yesterday seem like an illusion.
text The bright light is softened by the curtains as it reaches the wooden floor.
text She continues to slide the mop across the floor again and again.
text @[Tomoya]
text What do you do in the morning?
sound BVX.aac
text @[Kotomi]
text Lots of stuff at home.
text She answers while mopping.
text I wonder if she means she does housework.
text Since she makes her own lunch boxes, I'm sure she keeps her house in order.
text @[Tomoya]
text Uh-huh. It must be a lot of trouble.
sound BVY.aac
text @[Kotomi]
text Yeah.
text @[Tomoya]
text Have you ever hung out with others?
sound BVZ.aac
text @[Kotomi]
text Yes...
text Her answers are vague, possibly because her attention is focused on cleaning.
text She's mopping an even larger area than before.
text I'm staring at her in a daze.
text After a while, she finally finishes cleaning.
text She puts away the mop and brings out her cushion.
text She takes a pile of books out of her bag and puts them on the table.
text Picking out each book one by one, she makes a circle on the ground.
text She dusts off her cushion and throws it in the middle of the circle.
sound BW0.aac
text @[Kotomi]
text Here we go... here we go...
text She stands on one leg to take off a sock.
sound BW1.aac
text @[Kotomi]
text Whoa...
text She almost trips and hops around on one leg.
sound BW2.aac
text @[Kotomi]
text Phew... here we go...
text She manages to become barefoot.
text Now she's ready.
text Why am I staring at her?
text Wasn't I going to find an empty classroom to kill time in?
text Looking at things objectively, aren't I just in her way?
text @[Tomoya]
text ...
text Weird feelings are welling up inside of me.
text Feelings of nostalgia and guilt are mixing deep inside my mind.
text I think I've experienced these exact emotions before.
text I think it was...
